## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical implementation of privacy safeguards in Azure OpenAI within multi-tenant SaaS, focusing on data leakage prevention, RBAC, and auditable logging.

## Key Concepts
- PII detection and redaction pipelines
- Grounding with Cognitive Search over a versioned KB
- Per-tenant RBAC with Azure AD
- Data Lake auditing
- GDPR/CCPA compliance checks and synthetic-data tests

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: redaction before OpenAI call
async function process(input, tenantId) {
  const pii = detectPII(input);
  const redacted = redact(input, pii);
  const prompt = buildPrompt(redacted, tenantId);
  return await openai.complete(prompt);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you verify no PII leaks in logs or prompts across tenants?
- What metrics ensure latency remains acceptable under load?

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes end-to-end thinking on governance, data lineage, and drift in a multi-tenant Azure OpenAI deployment.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-tenant policy enforcement and data residency
- Drift detection across prompts and retrieved knowledge
- Data lineage with Azure Purview and observability with Azure Monitor
- PII redaction before OpenAI calls and grounding with Cognitive Search

## Code Example
```javascript
function redactPII(text){
  // naive: redact an email-like token if present
  if (text.indexOf('@') >= 0) {
    const at = text.indexOf('@')
    const left = text.substring(0, at)
    return left + '[REDACTED_EMAIL]'
  }
  return text
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you implement the drift alert rule and rollback workflow in Azure Monitor?
- What tests would you automate to validate PII redaction and policy gating across tenants?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to design a practical, beginner-friendly multi-tenant flow with prompt catalog versioning, failover, and privacy controls in Azure OpenAI.

## Key Concepts

- API Management routing with tenant context
- Versioned prompt catalog stored in Azure Blob
- Per-tenant quotas and graceful fallback
- PII redaction via Text Analytics before OpenAI calls
- Regional OpenAI endpoints and observability

## Code Example

```javascript
async function routeRequest(tenantId, payload) {
  const tmpl = await blob.get(`prompts/${tenantId}/v1.json`);
  const redacted = pii.redact(payload.prompt, payload.user);
  const finalPrompt = `${tmpl.promptPrefix}\n${redacted}`;
  return openai.chat(finalPrompt);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test failover if the catalog fetch fails?
- How would you monitor per-tenant quotas and trigger alerts?

## Why This Is Asked

Assess practical integration of Azure OpenAI with tenant-aware access control, data lineage, and auditable logging in a live analytics platform.

## Key Concepts

- Azure OpenAI + policy engine for data access
- Tenant-scoped RBAC with Azure AD
- Grounding against versioned KB in Azure Blob via Cognitive Search
- Purview lineage and Data Lake auditing
- Data leakage guardrails and synthetic-scenario testing

## Code Example

```javascript
function buildQuery(userInput) {
  // Use parameterized queries to prevent injection
  const sql = "SELECT * FROM orders WHERE owner_id = @owner AND region = @region";
  const params = { owner: userInput.owner, region: userInput.region };
  return { sql, params };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

